-- Sunken Temple, the Temple of Atal'Hakkar (map 109): the plan for the run leader (.bot run), exported from turtle-agent
-- prep/sunken_temple e63e6ab (dungeons/sunken_temple.json, status 'draft (not mapped, not live-checked)') with
--   turtle-agent plan-export --mmaps <map 109 mmaps> --allow-draft --gm-cross-direct --approach-hops --rev e63e6ab \
--     --stamp 20261023130200 --out <dir> sunken_temple
-- Stacks on 20261023120000. NO ROW IS HAND-SET beyond the plan file (the exporter wrote every row). The census behind the
-- plan edits is ~/TortoiseBots-audit/PREP-SUNKEN-TEMPLE-2026-10-23.md ("Fixes applied"):
--   * plan row lists: cc_priority 5259,5273,5269,5226 (the healers 5259/5273/5269 and the Slowing Poison 5226), cc_always 5259
--     (the Witch Doctor: Healing Wave, Hex, Chain Lightning), kill_first 5271,5280,5291 (Fear, Sleep, Frostbolt Volley with the
--     Swoop summon). fleers 5259,5273 (EventAI command 47 at 15 %) are in the plan only: the rows have no column.
--   * radii: leg 0 pull group 5 is 17.5 (was 27.0; it reached the 8311 of group 6 at 26.8 yd), leg 3 groups 2 and 3 are
--     14.3 and 15.6 (were 24.1 and 25.2; each reached the other's 5263/5271/5273 at 14.4-22.7 yd), and the seven single
--     Hakkari Frostwing 5291 pulls are 17 yd (its wander is 15: at the exporter's 10 the pull could find nothing).
-- 6 legs, 1365 steps, 1372 rows: 89 pulls (16 + 37 + 25 + 8 + 2 + 1), 6 boss rows (Atal'alarion 8580, Weaver 5720,
-- Dreamscythe 5721, Jammal'an the Prophet 5710 with Ogom 5711 as `first`, Morphaz 5719 with Hazzas 5722 as `first`, Shade of
-- Eranikus 5709, in leg order) and 1270 move rows. Plan check (map 109 mmaps): ok, 319 points, 23 detour warnings (packs 25-45
-- yd away by 83-1020 yd ways: the tank finds no firing position; stand the party on the pack's own layer) and 82 run-leader hop
-- notices (a pull or boss 50-217 yd from the move row before it). 1055 of the 1270 move rows are cut approach paths.
--
-- BLOCKER before a first live run (the data, not a row problem): the instance script (instance_sunken_temple.cpp) sets
-- Weaver 5720 and Dreamscythe 5721 VISIBILITY_OFF and not selectable until TYPE_JAMMALAN is DONE, and Atal'alarion 8580
-- VISIBILITY_OFF until the six Atal'ai statues are lit in order. This plan's leg order fights the Weaver and Dreamscythe boss
-- rows (legs 1 and 2) before the Jammal'an leg (leg 3), and it has no statue use step, so the leg 0, 1 and 2 boss rows cannot
-- finish as ordered (the run leader waits 60 s, then pauses "boss not found"). Fixing it is a plan reorder / event steps: a
-- behaviour change for the maintainer, not part of this export.
--
-- WHAT THE RUN LEADER CANNOT DO (issue #984: nothing is dropped silently). Not in these rows:
--   * fleers 5259,5273: no column; the bots' own AI chases or lets go a fleeing mob.
--   * the patrols: 5708 Spawn of Hakkar (guids 33621 and 34520, 12-point `creature_movement` paths spanning about 190 yd) and
--     Murk Worm 5226 (guids 33676 with 46 points and 34168 with 4) walk through the halls. A row carries no path, so a pull of
--     one of them can find nothing at its point (read as "pack cleared") and they can join later fights.
--   * the six-statue event (GO_ATALAI_STATUE_1-6 in the order S, N, SW, SE, NW, NE): no use_object steps; Atal'alarion stays
--     hidden. The six troll mini-bosses 5712-5717 (the statues' guards) ARE pulls of legs 1 and 2.
--   * the four Eternal Flames (148418-148421) and the Avatar of Hakkar 8443 (no spawn row): no steps, no boss row.
--   * Jammal'an's barrier (149431) opens when the six protectors 5712-5717 are dead (the instance does it); the Hakkar doors
--     149432/149433 belong to the Avatar event. No door step is needed for the barrier, and none is in the rows.
--   * Shade of Eranikus 5709 is not selectable until TYPE_JAMMALAN is DONE (leg 3), which is before its leg 5 row; he needs no
--     Essence of Eranikus item for that unlock in this core.
--   * the entrance (trigger 446 "Sunken Temple - Entrance", required level 35, portal map 0 -10162.7 -3998.65 -107.978),
--     level_band 47-52 and hire_composition: the run leader starts inside the instance and leads the bound party as it is.
--
-- Dungeon plans for the run leader (.bot run), exported by turtle-agent (plan-export). Plan format v1; the mapping is
-- docs/guides/dungeon-run-leader.md ("From plan v1 to rows"). The plan file in turtle-agent is the single source: edit it
-- there and export again, never these rows by hand. The plan row carries the unit lists cc_priority, cc_always and kill_first
-- (columns from 20261015200000_world.sql). Never edit this file once applied; export a new one.
--
-- Idempotent: each plan's rows are deleted, then inserted. The tables come from 20261014150000_world.sql.

-- sunken_temple: map 109, 6 legs, 1365 steps
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_step` WHERE `plan` = 'sunken_temple';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_leg` WHERE `plan` = 'sunken_temple';
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_plan` WHERE `plan` = 'sunken_temple';

-- Dungeon bosses of map 109, for the commander telemetry's boss rank (see 20261021114931_world.sql): the six boss steps'
-- entries, read from Turtle's own world data (tortoise-wow sql/base creature_template: all six are rank 1 there). The DELETE is
-- scoped to this plan's own entries, not the whole map, so a later map-109 plan's rows survive. No other plan on map 109 exists
-- in this repo yet; the scope is the rule the four SM wings use on map 189.
DELETE FROM `ai_dungeon_boss` WHERE `map` IN (109) AND `entry` IN (8580, 5720, 5721, 5710, 5719, 5709);
